 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Taking over as acting chef, Fedya tries to win the kitchen's hearts by announcing a break with free cream coffee for everyone except his rival Senya. When a waitress brings an order for medallions, Fedya refuses to let his crew work.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "sveta",
   "t": "Кофе со сливками специально для вас.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Прошу внимания, вся наша команда!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Как старший объявляю сейчас перерыв.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Кофе со сливками всем бесплатно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Ну, разумеется, кроме нашего Сени.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Своих конкурентов я не угощаю.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Вы коня моего не видели?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "А вы в шкафчике посмотрите.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "sveta",
   "t": "Нужны горячие медальоны для гостя.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Вообще-то у нас законный перерыв.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Я людям перерабатывать не дам.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "sveta",
   "t": "Хорошо, я так и передам.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "sveta",
   "t": "Кофе со сливками специально для вас.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Coffee with cream especially for you.' Sveta chooses one loaded word for Fedya: \"slivkami\" means \"cream\" (from \"slivki\"), giving the line its exact edge.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Прошу внимания, вся наша команда!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Attention please, our entire team!' Fedya stands firm earnestly to be clear, before Sveta can change the subject.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Как старший объявляю сейчас перерыв.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'As senior chef I declare a break now.' Fedya fires back bluntly with a shrug, watching Senya's face to see how the news lands.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Кофе со сливками всем бесплатно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Coffee with cream for everyone for free.' Fedya highlights one vivid word right here: \"slivkami\" means \"cream\" (from \"slivki\"), giving the line its exact edge.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Ну, разумеется, кроме нашего Сени.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Well, of course, except for our Senya.' Fedya replies calmly without holding back, letting the remark speak for itself.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Своих конкурентов я не угощаю.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I do not treat my competitors.' Fedya responds plainly with Sveta, leaving no doubt about where he stands.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Вы коня моего не видели?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Have you seen my horse?' Senya features one vivid term in earnest: \"konya\" means \"horse, knight\", and it carries the main weight of what Senya is saying.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "А вы в шкафчике посмотрите.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Take a look inside the locker.' Fedya chooses this telling touch in earnest: \"shkafchike\" means \"evochka\", and it carries the main weight of what Fedya is saying.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "sveta",
   "t": "Нужны горячие медальоны для гостя.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Hot medallions are needed for a guest.' Sveta stands firm steadily in this moment, before Fedya can change the subject.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Вообще-то у нас законный перерыв.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Actually, we are on a legal break.' Fedya anchors one vivid detail for Sveta: \"voobshche-to\" means \"actually\", and it carries the main weight of what Fedya is saying.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Я людям перерабатывать не дам.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I will not let my people overwork.' Fedya cuts in boldly as things stand, shifting the whole mood of the room in a single beat.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "sveta",
   "t": "Хорошо, я так и передам.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Fine, I will pass that along.' Sveta pushes back evenly beside Senya, steering the talk right where she wants it.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
